---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import MediaCredit from "../components/MediaCredit.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
import { asset } from "../data/paths";
---

<Layout title={`Accessibility & media credits — ${site.wordmark}`}>
  <div class="reading-container">
    <header class="page-title">
      <p class="eyebrow">Access & attribution</p>
      <h1>Accessibility & media credits</h1>
      <p class="lead">The design target is WCAG 2.1 Level A and AA.</p>
      <p>Semantic HTML, visible keyboard focus, descriptive media alternatives, and responsive layouts support access. Automated checks do not establish complete ADA or WCAG conformance.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <section>
        <h2>Using this site</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>The first keyboard link skips to the main content. All links, video controls, and expandable descriptions are keyboard operable.</li>
          <li>Silent videos can play and loop when visible. Use each player’s native controls to pause or resume. Videos pause outside the viewport; returning does not override a manual pause.</li>
          <li>Reduced-motion and data-saving preferences prevent automatic playback. Explicit native playback remains available.</li>
          <li>Every video has a complete text alternative and a timed WebVTT description track. The local video files contain no audio tracks.</li>
          <li>Complete media frames appear below the title and stack on narrow screens. The page reflows at narrow widths and with increased text spacing.</li>
          <li>Research figures have alt text and expandable explanations. The homepage presents qualitative findings; numerical result displays are omitted.</li>
          <li>Core content, descriptions, and native player controls remain available without JavaScript. BibTeX can be selected and copied manually.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Research and presentation scope</h2>
        <p>The published paper evaluates a learned policy in simulated urban flight. It does not include real-aircraft trials, takeoff, landing, or operating certification. Comfort, safety, and noise depend on the study’s models; results do not establish generalization to arbitrary changing winds.</p>
        <p>The authors’ <cite>Flying DNA - Copy 1.pptx</cite> introduces a broader vision spanning digital twins, connected systems, and artificial intelligence. Its city and wind illustrations do not establish a specific test condition. The title video and the body excerpts come from the same slide animation; they do not demonstrate or validate the published policy.</p>
        <p>The NASA/Joby title footage provides independent real-flight context. It is separate from the authors’ simulation and does not demonstrate their controller.</p>
      </section>
      <section id="attachments">
        <h2>Paper and source materials</h2>
        <p>The <a href={site.paperUrl}>published paper</a> contains the complete methods and numerical findings. Access to the version of record may depend on the publisher’s access rights.</p>
        <p>The original manuscript and source data remain unchanged. The supplied PDF reports tags, but tag presence alone does not verify heading structure, figure alternatives, equation reading, or reading order. External PDF and screen-reader behavior have not been certified.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Related work</h2>
        <p><a href="https://arxiv.org/html/2609.36056v1">GeoWind2Plan</a> is an independent study with an HTML reading version. Its findings are not presented as this project’s experiments. The external PDF is untagged; its reading order and assistive-technology behavior remain unverified.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Checks and remaining review</h2>
        <p>The repository checks axe-core WCAG 2.1 A/AA rules, native keyboard playback, persistent manual pause, reduced-motion and data-saving preferences, media descriptions, narrow-screen reflow, increased text spacing, and content without JavaScript. See <a href={`${site.siteRepo}/actions`}>the deployment checks</a> and <a href={`${site.siteRepo}/blob/main/ACCESSIBILITY.md`}>the accessibility review record</a>.</p>
        <p>Multiple screen-reader testing, review with users with disabilities, and institutional accessibility and brand review remain outside the completed technical checks. No complete ADA or WCAG certification is claimed.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Report an access barrier</h2>
        <p>Email <a href="mailto:liusongyang@ufl.edu">Songyang Liu at liusongyang@ufl.edu</a> with the page, content needed, and browser or assistive technology involved.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Privacy</h2>
        <p>Fonts, figures, and videos load locally. This static site has no analytics, advertising, or embedded third-party players. External links open the provider’s site and are subject to its privacy practices.</p>
      </section>
    </div>
    <div class="section"><MediaCredit /></div>
    <section class="section">
      <h2>Research figure credits</h2>
      <p>The framework diagram comes from the published paper by {site.authors.map((a) => a.name).join(", ")}. The city and wind illustrations come from the authors’ Flying DNA presentation. Original diagram colors are retained; labels and text explanations communicate the information without requiring color identification.</p>
      <p>Full descriptions and credits are beside the <a href={asset("#method")}>method illustrations</a>. Rights in published papers and third-party media remain with their respective holders.</p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
